Economic inequality has widened sharply across major metropolitan areas since the 1980s [Source: ev-2].
  - Gini coefficient reached 0.40 by 2013, with many metros showing steeper increases [Source: ev-2].
  - New York City leads among cities with a Gini coefficient of 0.5469, while Atlanta and Miami are at 0.57 and New Orleans at 0.56 [Source: ev-2].
